\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


A conjecture is a proposed mathematical assertion. A surrogate is an efficiently computed quantity used to estimate a harder quantity. Formal proof assistants mechanically check derivations in their stated formal foundations.
\paragraph{Record scope and qualifications.}
The catalogue title is retained as metadata. Named certificates, contracts, bounds or frameworks in that title are not asserted as results of the original source extract.
The specific bounds, free-group action, and required mathematical guarantees are not supplied; workflow goals remain source-described research directions.

Source-record limitation: The hard quantities, proposed bounds, and free-group action are unspecified; the remaining items are workflow design.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Develop machine-guided methods that discover useful bounds between hard matrix quantities and efficiently computable surrogates; characterize invariants of free-group actions on spaces of conjectures; and integrate conjecture-generation pipelines with formal proof assistants and natural-language representations. \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2023/26}{[S2]}
\paragraph{Source status.}
The supplied catalogue labels this source record open; that metadata was checked against the supplied snapshot on 2026-10-11. The label is preserved for provenance and is not an independent verification of present open status or mathematical correctness. The catalogue literature assessment is dated 2026-08-22.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Use automated methods to generate useful conjectures and connect them to formal checking.

